WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.920
Agents can call your tools.

00:00:02.275 --> 00:00:04.785
But who decides which ones,
and for how long?

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.980
That is what MCP Runtime does.

00:00:10.275 --> 00:00:12.985
It is a control plane for MCP servers.

00:00:13.395 --> 00:00:14.845
Set it up with one command.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:16.280
Deploy a server.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.390
Then give an agent a grant,
with a time limit.

00:00:22.217 --> 00:00:23.387
Open the console.

00:00:23.747 --> 00:00:25.577
Here are your servers and their tools.

00:00:25.942 --> 00:00:27.512
Here are the grants and sessions.

00:00:27.947 --> 00:00:31.917
And here, every call the gateway checked,
including the denied ones.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:35.860
Your infrastructure.

00:00:36.265 --> 00:00:37.075
Your rules.

00:00:37.475 --> 00:00:40.645
Open source,
with a hosted preview you can try today.

